WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.050
You do not rob your neighbors.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.750
You do not threaten them.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.310
Neither does Dan.

4
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.850
Dan is the man on your street who lends out his ladder.

5
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:16.930
Then one spring Ruth, across the road, digs up her front lawn to grow vegetables.

6
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.830
Dan thinks it drags the whole street down.

7
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.970
He watches the bean poles go up from his porch, and says nothing.

8
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.554
He would never walk over and make her stop.

9
00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:30.394
Dan already lives by a plain idea.

10
00:00:30.394 --> 00:00:36.394
Every adult has agency: the capacity to act for yourself and to make agreements.

11
00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:38.814
And you can lend it to someone else.

12
00:00:38.814 --> 00:00:43.034
When Dan's daughter bought her first car, he co-signed the loan.

13
00:00:43.034 --> 00:00:45.694
His name went on the paper under hers.

14
00:00:45.694 --> 00:00:46.974
She drives it.

15
00:00:46.974 --> 00:00:48.594
She makes the payments.

16
00:00:48.594 --> 00:00:51.634
If she ever stops, the bank calls Dan.

17
00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:55.254
That is how agency works: someone else acts,

18
00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.914
and you stay responsible for what they do.

19
00:00:57.914 --> 00:01:00.434
A vote is that kind of signature.

20
00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.204
It goes on what the candidate promised to do.

21
00:01:04.104 --> 00:01:06.184
You would not steal from your neighbor.

22
00:01:06.184 --> 00:01:09.684
You would not send another neighbor to do it for you, either.

23
00:01:09.684 --> 00:01:12.744
And if you did, you would answer for it.

24
00:01:12.744 --> 00:01:17.284
Dan would never pay the man next door to pull up Ruth's beans in the night.

25
00:01:17.284 --> 00:01:19.624
Sending someone is not a loophole.

26
00:01:20.524 --> 00:01:23.744
Except in one place, where it feels like one.

27
00:01:23.744 --> 00:01:28.184
That autumn a candidate for the town council knocks on Dan's door.

28
00:01:28.184 --> 00:01:32.244
She promises tidy streets, and she gets his vote.

29
00:01:32.244 --> 00:01:36.164
Your representatives, on the town council or in Congress,

30
00:01:36.164 --> 00:01:39.124
are neighbors to whom you delegate your agency.

31
00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:41.844
They win it by promising to solve problems.

32
00:01:41.844 --> 00:01:45.304
And they hold a tool no other neighbor has.

33
00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:51.024
The sociologist Max Weber defined the state by it: a monopoly on the legitimate use

34
00:01:51.024 --> 00:01:51.912
of force.

35
00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.112
Now watch the promise being kept.

36
00:01:55.112 --> 00:01:58.692
In April a notice is taped to Ruth's door.

37
00:01:58.692 --> 00:02:01.412
Ruth reads it, and goes on planting.

38
00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:04.652
In June a fine comes through the letter slot.

39
00:02:04.652 --> 00:02:06.952
In July, a larger one.

40
00:02:06.952 --> 00:02:08.612
Then a court order.

41
00:02:08.612 --> 00:02:11.572
And behind the court order, an officer.

42
00:02:11.572 --> 00:02:13.632
Ruth does not wait for him.

43
00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:17.012
One evening she pulls up the bean poles herself.

44
00:02:17.012 --> 00:02:22.812
Most people give in long before the last step, which is why it is easy to forget.

45
00:02:22.812 --> 00:02:25.992
But the last step is what makes the first one work.

46
00:02:25.992 --> 00:02:28.572
And the first step was Dan's vote.

47
00:02:28.572 --> 00:02:30.357
He never crossed the road.

48
00:02:31.257 --> 00:02:34.297
Tell Dan this, and he has a strong reply.

49
00:02:34.297 --> 00:02:35.657
I did nothing.

50
00:02:35.657 --> 00:02:36.957
I voted.

51
00:02:36.957 --> 00:02:41.497
Everyone had a say, the majority chose, and it is the law.

52
00:02:41.497 --> 00:02:44.897
Besides, my one vote decided nothing.

53
00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.737
Take that seriously.

54
00:02:46.737 --> 00:02:49.597
A vote settles who gets to decide.

55
00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:53.217
It does not change what arrives at the other end.

56
00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:58.297
Ruth, on her knees in that garden, feels what anyone feels when they are made to

57
00:02:58.297 --> 00:03:03.497
obey: less happy, with a grievance against whoever sent it.

58
00:03:03.497 --> 00:03:05.857
And one vote among thousands?

59
00:03:05.857 --> 00:03:11.337
Say ten neighbors each put in fifty dollars to pay a man to pull up Ruth's beans.

60
00:03:11.337 --> 00:03:13.617
None of them decided it alone.

61
00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:15.493
Every one of them paid for it.

62
00:03:16.393 --> 00:03:19.213
Two years later the council changes hands.

63
00:03:19.213 --> 00:03:24.173
The new majority promised quiet weekends, and Ruth voted for them.

64
00:03:24.173 --> 00:03:28.113
Dan rebuilds old engines in his driveway on Saturdays.

65
00:03:28.113 --> 00:03:30.953
In May a notice is taped to his door.

66
00:03:30.953 --> 00:03:33.473
It looks exactly like hers.

67
00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:37.793
That is the trouble with this loophole: it is open to everyone.

68
00:03:37.793 --> 00:03:40.293
Whatever you can send to a neighbor's door,

69
00:03:40.293 --> 00:03:44.989
the neighbor who disagrees with you can send to yours, as soon as their side wins.

70
00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:47.769
None of this is about guilt.

71
00:03:47.769 --> 00:03:50.569
It is about what you are building for yourself.

72
00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:55.749
Make it something you care about far more than a lawn, and the chain is the same,

73
00:03:55.749 --> 00:03:57.509
whichever side you are on.

74
00:03:57.509 --> 00:04:02.549
Liberal values and conservative values are both good values to live by.

75
00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:07.909
But nearly every party advances its values the same way: by making the people who

76
00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:10.069
do not share them comply.

77
00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:13.969
And each is counting on nobody following the chain to its end.

78
00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:15.724
Now you have.

79
00:04:16.624 --> 00:04:21.684
So before you lend your name, ask yourself the question Dan never asked.

80
00:04:21.684 --> 00:04:24.064
Am I comfortable co-signing this?

81
00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.544
One last look at Dan.

82
00:04:26.544 --> 00:04:28.724
His complaint was real to him.

83
00:04:28.724 --> 00:04:32.244
And in two years he never once crossed the road.

84
00:04:32.244 --> 00:04:35.495
Not to threaten Ruth, and not to talk to her either.

85
00:04:36.395 --> 00:04:38.495
Which leaves the obvious worry.

86
00:04:38.495 --> 00:04:40.295
A lawn is small.

87
00:04:40.295 --> 00:04:44.275
The big problems are real, and people need help now.

88
00:04:44.275 --> 00:04:47.935
If no one is forced, how does anything get solved?

89
00:04:47.935 --> 00:04:51.715
That is next: Cooperation Is a Technology.

90
00:04:51.715 --> 00:04:55.837
The whole series, in order, is at humanrespect.app.
